  "id": "Compound::DB00222 - Gene::3758",
  "verbalization": "Glimepiride, a sulfonylurea antidiabetic agent, is implicated in its interaction with Kcnj1 through a shared pathway involving sulfonylurea compounds. Both Glimepiride and Glyburide, which are included in the Sulfonylurea Compounds class, bind to Kcnj1, suggesting a common mechanism of action. The lowest common ancestor of Glimepiride and its metabolites, such as Tolbutamide and Glyburide, points to the broader category of N-Sulfonylureas, which are known to interact with potassium channels, including Kcnj1. This binding likely occurs through a shared pharmacological mechanism, where sulfonylureas modulate potassium channels, potentially influencing cellular electrical activity. The evidence from both paths supports a role for Glimepiride in modulating Kcnj1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
